  "id": "end-aversion-bias",
  "term": "end-aversion bias",
  "definition": "End-aversion bias is a measurement bias that can occur in visual analogue scale (VAS) preference ratings. It means the validity of the rating may be influenced by reluctance or distortion related to the scale’s endpoints or anchors.",
